CyberArk / IDIRA Issues Identified

1.	Requester and Approver Role Conflict
The team requested membership in both the Requester and Approver groups for applications configured with an approval workflow. However, this configuration allows users who hold both roles to approve their own application access requests. The team considers this a concern and would prefer approvers not self approve their own request.

2.	Salesforce Session Timeout Not Enforced by IDIRA
Salesforce application sessions are not terminating based on the expected timeout period. The session lifecycle and timeout behavior appear to be controlled by Salesforce rather than CyberArk IDIRA, meaning the IDIRA configuration does not currently enforce termination of the active Salesforce session.


3.	Permanent Access Option Visible to Requesters
When requesting access to an application through IDIRA, users are presented with both permanent and time-bound access options. The team does not want requesters to have the ability to select permanent access and would prefer that users only be presented with a windowed/time-bound access option.

4.	SWS Session Recording Does Not Distinguish Application Users
SWS session recording appears to associate activity with the same application session when users access the application through the same URL. As a result, the recording does not appear to clearly differentiate sessions based on the individual application username being used, creating a potential limitation in user-level session traceability and recording attribution.
